From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 01:39:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] portal: in-place rnsd update (pip) + pip/setuptools on
 the rootfs

Builds on the update-check notifier with an actual in-place update, since the
rootfs is writeable and rns is a pure-Python wheel. updatecheck.apply_update()
installs the latest rns wheel with pip (--no-deps --only-binary, so the
compiled deps cryptography/pyserial are never rebuilt), first clearing the old
buildroot (distutils) install that pip cannot uninstall, keeping a rollback
tarball, and restarting + verifying rnsd -- rolling back automatically if rnsd
does not come back. Only site-packages is touched; /etc and user config are
never modified. A dependency pre-check refuses the update (pointing at a
reflash) if the new rns needs a newer cryptography/pyserial than is installed.
(pip 22.3.1 on the target predates --break-system-packages, and buildroot's
rootfs is not PEP-668 externally-managed, so no such flag is used.)

The Reticulum tab gains an "Update rnsd to X now" button (with a confirm) when
an update is available, via a new /reticulum/applyupdate route. Enables
python-pip + python-setuptools in the defconfig so pip is on the box for this
and for general package management.
